  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "Direct L1 oral-bioavailability outcomes for anthranilic acid NSAIDs and related acids are high: meclofenamate >85% (C06), diflunisal 89.5% (C10), flufenamic acid good (C02), and telmisartan 42-58% (C01, C03), supporting F>=20% for the query's acidic scaffold.",
      "card_ids": ["C06", "C10", "C02", "C01", "C03"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Sulfonamide-containing drugs also meet the F>=20% threshold: celecoxib 20-40% (C07), pazopanib 21.4% (C13), and BMS-275183 24% (C22), indicating that the sulfonamide moiety does not by itself place the query below threshold.",
      "card_ids": ["C07", "C13", "C22"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 low-permeability records do not establish low F: salicylic acid is low in PAMPA (C135) yet diflunisal, a salicylic acid derivative, has F 89.5% (C10); mefenamic acid, an anthranilic acid, has low PAMPA at 5% EPO (C162) while anthranilic acid NSAIDs have high F (C06, C02); HCTZ low PAMPA (C136) is not a direct F outcome.",
      "card_ids": ["C135", "C10", "C162", "C06", "C02", "C136"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 records for ionized acids and sulfonamide-containing drugs show adequate solubility/absorption: diclofenac sodium solubility 2.43 g/L and intestinal permeability 10e-6 cm/s (C131), tamsulosin >90% absorbed (C147) and 100% absorbed (C153), and chlorothiazide solubility 3.1 mg/mL at pH 8 (C165).",
      "card_ids": ["C131", "C147", "C153", "C165"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "No L4 record provides a direct furosemide F or permeability value; C178 only used furosemide at 1 mM in a Caco-2 assay without reporting furosemide Papp. Low permeability for sulfasalazine (C148) is a prodrug context and is not a transferable direct low-F outcome.",
      "card_ids": ["C178", "C148"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "intestinal_absorption_permeability",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C131", "C147", "C153", "C165", "C135", "C162", "C148", "C136", "C155", "C166", "C167", "C178"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct furosemide-specific permeability, solubility, or fraction-absorbed record was supplied; C178 mentions furosemide only as a 1 mM Caco-2 incubation reagent.",
    "No cystic fibrosis-specific pharmacokinetic data were supplied; extrapolation from general human and animal populations is indirect.",
    "L4 records report in vitro permeability/solubility for related molecules, not absolute F for the query, so they inform but do not directly quantify bioavailability.",
    "First-pass metabolism and gut-wall extraction for the query are not directly measured; L5 may address this.",
    "Furosemide formulation-dependent and dose-dependent absorption variability is not directly captured."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Prediction remains high (F>=20%). L1 direct bioavailability outcomes for anthranilic acid NSAIDs and related acids are high, and L4 low-permeability records for salicylic acid, mefenamic acid, HCTZ, and sulfasalazine do not establish F<20% because low in vitro permeability can coexist with high oral F and no direct furosemide F or permeability value was supplied. L4 solubility/absorption records for ionized acids and sulfonamide drugs are consistent with meaningful absorption. Confidence remains moderate."
}

